Id: upd010w
Severity: WARN
Category: packages
Check: check_updates
Fix: Add the release's security suite (<codename>-security) to apt's sources and run apt update.
References: sources.list(5); https://www.debian.org/security/; https://ubuntu.com/security/notices
Controls: CIS 7.3, 7.4; NIST SI-2; ISO 8.8; CE Security update management

apt's sources name the release (Debian's or Ubuntu's codename) but no
security suite for it, so security updates never reach this host: the
point releases and -updates carry them weeks later, if at all. Nor can
Tigris count the security updates waiting (upd003f), since apt knows
of none; without this finding the silence would read as all patched.

The sources read are /etc/apt/sources.list and the .list and .sources
(deb822) files in /etc/apt/sources.list.d that apt reads; a comment,
a deb-src line and a stanza with 'Enabled: no' count for nothing. The
security suite is <codename>-security (on Debian, from
security.debian.org/debian-security or deb.debian.org/debian-security;
on Ubuntu, from security.ubuntu.com or any mirror), Ubuntu Pro's
<codename>-infra-security, or <codename>/updates, Debian's name for it
until buster. The release comes from os-release: UBUNTU_CODENAME on
Ubuntu and its derivatives (Mint, Pop!_OS), DEBIAN_CODENAME on LMDE.
Debian testing and sid are not judged (their os-release has no
VERSION_ID): their security support is not that of a release. Nor are
other Debian descendants (Raspbian publishes its fixes in the release
suite itself), nor a release no source names.

To fix it, add the suite, for Debian 12:

    deb http://security.debian.org/debian-security bookworm-security main

or, in /etc/apt/sources.list.d/debian.sources:

    Types: deb
    URIs: http://security.debian.org/debian-security
    Suites: bookworm-security
    Components: main
    Signed-By: /usr/share/keyrings/debian-archive-keyring.gpg

and on Ubuntu 24.04, 'noble-security' beside 'noble' and
'noble-updates' in /etc/apt/sources.list.d/ubuntu.sources; then run
'apt update'.
